# Line endings, settled once.
#
# This checkout runs with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, and the repo had no
# .gitattributes at all — so every file's line endings were whatever the
# working tree happened to produce. The visible cost was `prettier --check .`
# failing locally on files CI (LF) considered fine, which trained everyone to
# ignore a red format check and check only their own changed files by hand. A
# check you have learned to disbelieve is worse than no check.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalizes every text file to LF in the repository,
# regardless of what any one machine checks out. Binaries are listed
# explicitly: `text=auto` guesses well but a wrong guess on a font or an image
# corrupts it, and there is no reason to leave that to inference.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
